{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.QuantumObservableUniverseExists","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.QuantumObservableUniverseExists","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.CategoricalFoundations"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.exists_instance","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.exists_instance","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe-exists.lean#L92-L100","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:quantum-observable-universe-exists","label":"prop:quantum-observable-universe-exists","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe-exists.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverseExistsContext.exists_instance","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverseExistsContext.exists_instance","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe-exists.lean#L89-L89","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverseExistsContext.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverseExistsContext.mk","kind":"ctor","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe-exists.lean#L84-L84","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverseExistsContext","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QuantumObservableUniverseExistsContext","kind":"class","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/quantum-observable-universe-exists.lean#L64-L89","doc":"**Existence of a quantum observable universe over a commutative ring.**\n\n`R` is a commutative ring carrying a substrate parameter `q` with named\ninverse `qinv`, subject to the three conditions the cited construction\nneeds: `q − qinv` invertible (for the `q`-Casimir), `6` invertible and `q`\nWenzl-generic at every rank (for semisimplicity of `H_n(q)` via Jimbo).\n\n`hgeneric` is `∀ n, WenzlGeneric q n` written out — that definition\n(`QOU.Information.WenzlGeneric`, `∀ k, 2 ≤ k → k ≤ n → q ^ k ≠ 1`) is\nalready stated over a generic monoid, so it applies to `R` unchanged.  It\nis spelled inline rather than imported: `PNeqNpEquivalence` is a heavy\nInformation-chapter module and this is a content-block sibling, so pulling\nit in for one `Prop` would bloat the import cone.  Restating it as a\n*definition* here was the other option and is worse — a second\n`WenzlGeneric` is exactly the symbol collision the notation register warns\nabout.  Quantified over all `k` since `∀ n` makes the rank bound vacuous.\n\nWitnessed by Rep(SU_q(2)) with Haar integration, vanishing Chern classes on\nthe adjoint, and the quantum determinant volume constraint. ","signatureChunk":0}]}